<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meersburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meersburg is a small town on the north shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. After the city of Constance adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in the 1520s, the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Constance moved their residence there, later building a baroque New Palace beside the medieval Old Castle. The poet Annette von Droste-Hülshoff lived and died in the Old Castle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meersburg.jpg" alt="Meersburg" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hagar66 based on work of TUBS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meersburg_in_FN.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
